# Main checkout and stash — hands off

<!-- core -->
**Never write into a main checkout on its default branch** — no edit, stage, commit, stash or
reset there; work in a worktree and push. **Git stash is shared by every worktree:** never `git
stash pop/apply/drop/branch`, except on an explicit `stash@{N}` made on the current branch; if a
worktree looks wrong, stop and report BLOCKED with the exact `git status` output.

<!-- /core -->

## Why

The main checkout on its default branch is the landing target and a place to read from, never a
workbench: a session that edits, stages, commits, stashes or resets there leaves residue no later
session owns. The stash list is shared by every worktree of the repository, so an entry it names
implicitly may hold another change's work. The `block-unsafe-commands` hook
(`stats/internal/guard/hook/hookblockunsafecommands.go`) denies both; this rule is what holds where the
hook is not installed.
